# .env file — the most common place secrets leak in real deployments
# Run: harpocrates scan --ml user_test/samples/01_severity_calibration.env
#
# Expected severities (requires --ml for full classification pass):
#   APIM_CLIENT_KEY   → MEDIUM  (api_token lexicon, confidence 0.80)
#   APIM_SECRET_KEY   → MEDIUM  (secret_key lexicon, confidence 0.80)
#   DB_PASSWORD       → HIGH    (password lexicon, confidence 0.90)
#   JWT_BEARER_TOKEN  → HIGH    (jwt lexicon, confidence 0.85)
#   GENERIC_VAL       → INFO    (no strong var-name signal)
#
# None of these should appear as CRITICAL — that is reserved for regex-tier
# deterministic matches (e.g., a full AWS access key or GitHub PAT).

